BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginnings Summer Concert Series in Downtown Ithaca
DTSTART:20260813T210000Z
DTEND:20260814T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T101541Z
UID:ef57d5517cddd07bb61b94b922455c6946d26aa4@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Event by Downtown Ithaca\nBernie Milton Pavilion\n100 N. Tioga
  St.\nIthaca\, NY\nDuration: 3 hr\nPublic\nFree and fun for the entire fam
 ily\, the Beginnings Summer Concert Series brings live music to Downtown I
 thaca every Thursday at the Bernie Milton Pavilion. Local and national act
 s perform music in genres including jazz\, blues\, reggae\, folk\, hip hop
 \, country\, bluegrass\, rock\, and more.\nThursdays\, 5:00 PM – 8:00 PM
  at Bernie Milton Pavilion on the Ithaca Commons. This is a community-focu
 sed\, all-ages concert in the heart of downtown.\nEvent Dates & Performers
 :\n• June 11: Jill McCracken / Maddy Walsh & The Blind Spots\n• June 1
 8: Material Objects / Stranded with a Kiss / Eighteen Hundred and Froze to
  Death\n• June 25: Ariel Arbisser / SingTrece\n• July 2: Venissa Sant
 í / Jorge T. Cuevas & The Caribe Jazz Allstars\n• July 9: The Shambles 
 / Li’l Anne & Hot Cayenne\n• July 23: Kitestring / Caviar & Grits / Mi
 ke Powell & The Echosound\n• July 30: Louiston / Evan Horne\n• August 
 6: GIAC Jumpers & Southside Panthers / Fall Creek Brass Band\n• August 1
 3: Drew Kiddoo & The Blackouts / Miller and The Other Sinners\n• August 
 20: The Medicinals / Scuba Jerry\n• August 27: Jeremiah Craig / Cast Iro
 n Cowboys / The Rollin’ Rust\n• September 3: GIAC Jumpers & Southside 
 Panthers / Gunpoets\nFree outdoor performances every Thursday evening. Fam
 ily-friendly atmosphere in the center of downtown. A wide mix of genres fr
 om regional and national acts.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.t
 ime.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78416467/20260723170000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78416467/20260723170000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music in Centerway Square\, Corning
DTSTART:20260813T220000Z
DTEND:20260814T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T101541Z
UID:087a29409e9f6b2d3b839be89a6a6a1c2830cffa@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Dancing,Community,Family Fun,New to the Area
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to groove every Thursday night in July and August at
  Music in the Square! From 6 to 8 PM\, Centerway Square in downtown Cornin
 g transforms into the ultimate summer hangout with live performances by ta
 lented local and regional artists.\nWhether you're planning a romantic dat
 e night or a fun family outing\, this event has something for everyone. St
 roll through the historic streets of downtown Corning\, indulge in delicio
 us eats from local eateries\, and shop ‘til you drop before settling int
 o the charming atmosphere of Centerway Square. Let the music carry you thr
 ough the perfect summer evening in the heart of our vibrant community.\nAr
 tist Lineup:\nJuly 9\nDelta Blues by Gerard Burke\nBlues Guitarist\nJuly 1
 6\nSalsa Libre\nTraditional & Contemporary Latin Rhythms\nBonus: Free Sals
 a Dance Lesson with Latin Dance by Sandra Roig at 5:00 PM before the perfo
 rmance.\nJuly 23\nThe Variables\nClassic Rock\nJuly 30\nKira & The Kindnes
 s\nRock\, Funk\, Soul & Blues Fusion\nAugust 6\nBetter Halves\nCarissa For
 d & Thomas Andolino / Acoustic Covers\nAugust 13\nTBD\nAugust 20\nLouiston
 \nFolk & Roll Band\nAugust 27\nDisco Line Dancing Party with Rosita Wright
  & DJ Mark Schmidt\nGet your 80s on! Do the Hustle and hit the dance floor
  for a night of disco favorites\, line dancing\, and high-energy fun in Ce
 nterway Square! Learn a few moves\, groove with friends\, and celebrate th
 e end of the Music in the Square season.\nMark your calendars\, grab your 
 lawn chairs\, and join us for an unforgettable season of music and summer 
 vibes!\nThank you to our Summer in Downtown sponsor\, Williams Toyota.\n\n
 Source: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78407994/202
 60709180000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78407994/20260709180000
END:VEVENT
