BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Of Monsters and Men: The Mouse Parade Tour LIVE @ State Theatre of
  Ithaca
DTSTART:20260923T000000Z
DTEND:20260923T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T101541Z
UID:9a0527b0472bc6ec87bd493d9e7a0ad79009f560@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
DESCRIPTION:Event by State Theatre of Ithaca and DSP Shows\nState Theatre 
 of Ithaca\nPublic\nDSP Shows & the State Theatre of Ithaca Present:\nOf Mo
 nsters and Men - The Mouse Parade Tour\nwith August Ponthier\nTuesday\, Se
 ptember 22nd\, 2026\nDoors: 7pm | Show: 8pm\nTickets on sale Friday 7/10 @
  10am: https://tixr.com/e/19688\n_____________________________\nFrom Reykj
 avík to the global stage\, Of Monsters and Men (OMAM) first captured the 
 world’s attention with their 2011 debut My Head Is an Animal\, transform
 ing from Icelandic indie favorites into a band known and loved worldwide.\
 nBreakout single “Little Talks” became a generational anthem with over
  a billion Spotify streams and led to a 2013 Saturday Night Live debut. Th
 eir follow-up\, Beneath the Skin (2015)\, debuted Top 3 on the Billboard 2
 00 and included a surprise cameo on HBO’s Game of Thrones. Over the past
  15 years\, OMAM have continuously explored\, evolved\, and built a world 
 of music defi ned by growth and imagination—from the cinematic expansive
 ness of Beneath the Skin to the dreamlike textures of Fever Dream (2019).\
 nAlong the way\, OMAM’s cinematic sound has been featured in The Hunger 
 Games\, The Secret Life of Walter Mitty\, and more\, while commanding fest
 ival sets at Coachella\, Glastonbury\, and Lollapalooza cemented their rep
 utation as one of the most compelling live acts of their era. Their intima
 te pandemic-era documentary tíu (2022)\, which premiered at Tribeca and w
 on Best Short at Dumbo\, paired with an EP of unreleased tracks spanning a
  decade\, further showcased the depth and evolution of their craft.\nAfter
  pursuing solo and side projects\, the band now reunites with All Is Love 
 and Pain in the Mouse Parade\, a tapestry of stories\, moments\, and conve
 rsations\; the album explores how love and pain intertwine. Feelings that 
 might seem at odds with each other\, but co-exist simultaneously and need 
 one another. The album marks a new chapter in a career defined by growth\,
  exploration\, and a commitment to making music that reflects who they are
  today.\nWEB https://www.ofmonstersandmen.com/\nYOUTUBE https://www.youtub
 e.com/@monstersandmen\nINSTAGRAM https://www.instagram.com/ofmonstersandme
 n\nFACEBOOK https://www.facebook.com/ofmonstersandmen\nTIKTOK https://www.
 tiktok.com/@ofmonstersandmen\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.tim
 e.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78439061/20260922200000
GEO:42.439256;-76.499593
LOCATION:State Theatre of Ithaca\, 107 West State Street\, Ithaca\, New Yo
 rk\, 14850\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78439061/20260922200000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wisner Farmers Market in Elmira
DTSTART:20260923T140000Z
DTEND:20260923T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T101541Z
UID:10409a5aa64af331f9a463561f75a91b3cf61f81@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Farmers Market,Community,Music,Family Fun,New to the Area
DESCRIPTION:Downtown Elmira's beloved Wisner Market is back and better tha
 n ever. Join us every Wednesday in Wisner Park from 10:00 AM to 2:00 PM fo
 r a mid-week tradition that brings the community together all summer long.
 \nBrowse more than 30 vendors offering fresh produce\, cut flowers\, handm
 ade crafts\, unique local goods\, and more. Grab lunch from some of the be
 st food trucks and local restaurants in the area\, enjoy live music\, and 
 soak up everything that makes downtown Elmira special.\nLive Music Sponsor
